/-!
# The branch points `P_c = (c, 0)` of the hyperelliptic model and their ideal sheaves

Let `k` be a field and `f ∈ k[x]` separable. For a root `c` of `f`, `P_c = (c, 0)` is a point of
the finite chart `y^2 = f(x)` of the projective model `X = projectiveModel f`
(`ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Hyperelliptic.branchPoint`); the roots of `f` are exactly the
finite branch points
of the double cover `X → ℙ¹`
(`ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Hyperelliptic.isFiniteBranchPoint_iff`). This file
is the elementary half of `HyperellipticBranchDivisors`:

* `ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Divisors.pointIdeal P`: the ideal sheaf of a point (the vanishing
ideal sheaf
  of its closure); a section `s` over an affine open lies in it iff `P ∉ D(s)`
  (`ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Divisors.mem_pointIdeal_iff`).
* `ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Hyperelliptic.branchIdeal hc`: the ideal sheaf of `P_c`. On the
finite chart it
  is the maximal ideal `(x - c, y)` (`branchIdeal_ideal_chartOpen`), and its square is the
  principal ideal `(x - c)` (`branchIdeal_mul_self_ideal_chartOpen`, using that `f` is
  separable: `f/(x - c)` does not vanish at `c`); near `P_c` it is generated by `y`
  (`branchIdeal_ideal_basicOpen_divByMonic`), and the square is generated by the unit `1 - c/x`
  near infinity (`branchIdeal_mul_self_ideal_eq_span_of_le`).
* The local ratios `(x - c)/(1 - c/x) = x = (x - c')/(1 - c'/x)` on the overlap
  (`germ_branch_compat`).

The effective-Cartier and linear-equivalence statements, which need the Stacks divisor theory,
are in `ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials.Geometry.HyperellipticBranchDivisors`.
-/

public section

